  "articleBody": "When you're tackling mobile home door repairs, it's easy to make a few common blunders that can make things worse. First off, don't just measure the door slab itself! Mobile home interior doors often come in specific widths like 24, 28, or 30 inches, so you need to take careful rough-opening measurements. Another big mistake is ignoring hinge alignment. Even a slight misalignment can cause endless sticking and frustration. Always check for loose screws and consider using shims to correct any wobbly hinges. And whatever you do, don't leave old adhesive or damaged weatherstripping in place if you're replacing it. That stuff needs to go completely for a proper seal. Lastly, keep an eye out for moisture. Mobile home doors and trim can swell or move with the seasons, leading to sticking that might seem like a simple fix but could indicate a deeper moisture problem. If you're running into persistent issues, it's a good idea to get a pro involved before things get out of hand.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}